// local-spi1.repl — promotes SPI1 from a Tag to SPI.STM32H7_SPI.
//
// Upstream's stm32h7.repl leaves SPI1 as `Tag <0x40013000,...> "SPI1_/_I2S1"`
// while modelling spi4 with this same peripheral. Under the Tag, SPI_SR reads
// 0, so TXC never sets and the firmware cannot finish a transfer.
//
// The model alone is not enough: SPI transfers are DMA-backed and also need
// local-dma.repl. Load both through local-overlay.resc.
//
// STM32H7_SPI exposes both IRQ and DMARecieve, so the interrupt must be named
// explicitly -- a bare `-> nvic@35` is "Error E15: Ambiguous choice".
// DMARecieve is DMAMUX1 request 37 (SPI1_RX; the firmware programs 38, SPI1_TX, for the TX stream); without it
// the RX stream of transfer_in_place is never serviced. TX needs no request
// line: Renode's DMA runs memory-to-peripheral streams on enable.
spi1: SPI.STM32H7_SPI @ {
        sysbus 0x40013000;
        rcc RegistrationPeripheralAlias.SPI1
    }
    IRQ -> nvic@35
    DMARecieve -> dmamux1@37
